1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,324
Three questions.

2
00:00:01,544 --> 00:00:02,792
Can you get all three?

3
00:00:03,012 --> 00:00:03,978
Morning quiz!

4
00:00:04,698 --> 00:00:05,619
Question one.

5
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:06,770
The first line

6
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:07,502
is a defer.

7
00:00:07,722 --> 00:00:08,972
In what order do A,

8
00:00:08,972 --> 00:00:09,894
B and C print?

9
00:00:10,114 --> 00:00:11,211
Pause and answer.

10
00:00:11,931 --> 00:00:12,851
A, B, C.

11
00:00:13,071 --> 00:00:14,914
A deferred call waits until

12
00:00:14,914 --> 00:00:16,484
the function ends, so C

13
00:00:16,484 --> 00:00:18,327
prints last, even though it

14
00:00:18,327 --> 00:00:19,488
is written first.

15
00:00:20,208 --> 00:00:21,238
Question two.

16
00:00:21,458 --> 00:00:22,329
A new customer

17
00:00:22,329 --> 00:00:23,325
places an order.

18
00:00:23,545 --> 00:00:24,531
Do we add a new

19
00:00:24,531 --> 00:00:25,910
row, or a new column?

20
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:27,227
Pause and answer.

21
00:00:27,947 --> 00:00:28,791
A new row.

22
00:00:29,011 --> 00:00:29,999
One row is one

23
00:00:29,999 --> 00:00:31,622
record, here one order.

24
00:00:31,842 --> 00:00:33,189
A new column is only

25
00:00:33,189 --> 00:00:34,670
for a new detail, like

26
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:35,680
a phone number.

27
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,514
Interview question.

28
00:00:37,734 --> 00:00:39,263
In VLOOKUP, which last

29
00:00:39,263 --> 00:00:40,653
value gives an exact

30
00:00:40,653 --> 00:00:42,112
match, TRUE or FALSE?

31
00:00:42,332 --> 00:00:43,429
Pause and answer.

32
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:44,786
FALSE!

33
00:00:45,006 --> 00:00:46,590
FALSE means exact match.

34
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:48,829
TRUE means approximate, which can

35
00:00:48,829 --> 00:00:50,113
return the wrong row.

36
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,558
How many did you get?

37
00:00:51,778 --> 00:00:52,927
One, two or three?

38
00:00:53,147 --> 00:00:54,625
Follow CareerWithCode!

